WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.100
ApplyArc existed before. We built this standalone application during the hackathon.

2
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:11.496
Ellie's form asks what she did herself. These drafts were prepared earlier in this

3
00:00:11.496 --> 00:00:16.600
same hosted session. First, I save her own opening and approve both documents.

4
00:00:25.991 --> 00:00:31.299
Now her account changes. Sam wrote the patch. She reproduced the failure, tested his

5
00:00:31.299 --> 00:00:35.091
fix, and wrote the incident notes. I add that once.

6
00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:49.911
Wonder catches the conflict. The complete correction is already here. I check it and

7
00:00:49.911 --> 00:00:51.600
choose Use this correction.

8
00:00:57.300 --> 00:01:02.747
The agent proposes repairs in both documents. The project answer gives Sam credit and

9
00:01:02.747 --> 00:01:08.194
keeps Ellie's contribution. The cover letter also explains the failure, so the correction makes

10
00:01:08.194 --> 00:01:09.750
sense on its own.

11
00:01:24.190 --> 00:01:31.240
I review the changes before applying them. Her opening survives. Each updated document needs a fresh approval.

12
00:01:39.800 --> 00:01:44.992
Here is the finished letter, with its evidence beside it. I approve that version

13
00:01:44.992 --> 00:01:48.700
and open the pack. Both documents now reflect her correction.

14
00:01:53.766 --> 00:01:59.045
Nothing has been submitted. The employer's portal still needs the remaining steps. The applicant

15
00:01:59.045 --> 00:02:02.816
keeps control of the final words, and what happens next.
